NEARS-3436 QA — POST admin/order/add-to-cart / remove-from-cart response-shape evidence
Captured live via Playwright route interception against the worktree's own Admin server
(http://127.0.0.1:8001, worktree fix/NEARS-3436-add-to-cart-session-persist, disposable DB
clone multi_food_db_qa3436).

--- NON-FOOD BRANCH (order 91216, store 12 "Fresh local") ---
[add item53 "Hamburger Buns" (new, non-food)] ->
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/admin/order/add-to-cart -> 200 {"data":0}
  (new-item success shape unchanged; item persisted after reload)

[add item53 again (duplicate, same session)] ->
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/admin/order/add-to-cart -> 200 {"data":1}
  (duplicate-item shape unchanged; correctly blocked now that session actually holds the
  first add — pre-fix this check silently never fired since the cart was never persisted)

[add item62 "Oreo Choco Cookies" (different, legit, same session)] ->
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/admin/order/add-to-cart -> 200 {"data":0}
  (proves the duplicate check does not over-block a legitimately different item)

[edit item53 cart_item_key path, qty 1 -> 3] ->
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/admin/order/add-to-cart -> 200 {"data":2}
  (edit success shape unchanged; qty change persisted after reload — cart row showed "3 x")

[remove item62 via remove_from_cart] ->
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/admin/order/remove-from-cart -> 200 []
  (response shape unchanged; item removed from cart table after reload)

--- FOOD-VARIATION BRANCH (order 91133, store 4 "Burger Palace") ---
[add item16 "Classic Cheeseburger" variation Size=Regular (new, food)] ->
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/admin/order/add-to-cart -> 200 {"data":0}
  (new-item success shape unchanged; item + selected variation "Size - Regular"
  persisted after reload)

[edit item16 cart_item_key path, qty 1 -> 2] ->
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/admin/order/add-to-cart -> 200 {"data":2}
  (edit success shape unchanged; qty change persisted after reload — cart row showed
  "2 x د.إ. 8.99" = 17.98, variation retained)

[add item16 again with NO Size selected (variation-error early-return)] ->
  POST http://127.0.0.1:8001/admin/order/add-to-cart -> 200
  {"data":"variation_error","message":"Please select items from Size"}
  (variation-error shape unchanged; cart table text before/after this call byte-identical
  -> confirmed NO cart mutation on this early-return path)

--- FULL PLACE-ORDER / SUBMIT-EDIT-ORDER FLOW (regression sweep) ---
Order 91133 (food branch, 2-item cart: Veggie Burger qty1 @9.99 + Classic Cheeseburger
qty2 @8.99 w/ Size=Regular variation):
  on-screen total pre-submit: د.إ. 29.37
  after .submit-edit-order -> admin.order.update -> DB:
    orders.order_amount = 29.37, orders.total_tax_amount = 1.40
    order_details: (item 18 qty1 price 9.99, variation []),
                    (item 16 qty2 price 8.99, variation [{"name":"Size",...,"values":[{"label":"Regular","optionPrice":"0"}]}])
  MATCH: on-screen pre-submit total == finalized DB order_amount (29.37 == 29.37)

Order 91216 (non-food branch, 2-item cart: Brown Dinner Rolls qty1 @4.00 + Hamburger Buns
qty1 @4.00):
  on-screen total pre-submit: د.إ. 9.40
  after .submit-edit-order -> admin.order.update -> DB:
    orders.order_amount = 9.40, orders.total_tax_amount = 0.40
    order_details: (item 51 qty1 price 4.00), (item 53 qty1 price 4.00)
  MATCH: on-screen pre-submit total == finalized DB order_amount (9.40 == 9.40)

Conclusion: totals/tax compute correctly end-to-end through the full place-order/update
flow now that add_to_cart() actually persists the cart both branches feed from real,
session-backed multi-item carts (this path previously only ever saw an empty/stale cart
due to the NEARS-3436 bug).
